# 23. SECURITY BOUNDARY

================================================================================================================================

The current architecture establishes:

```text
Client
  ↓
Authenticated API
  ↓
Server user.id
  ↓
Server persistence helper
  ↓
Privileged database RPC
```

The client does not receive direct control over the database transaction.

The server derives the authenticated user's identity.

The database operation is scoped according to the authenticated user.

================================================================================================================================

# 24. IMPORTANT ARCHITECTURAL RULE

================================================================================================================================

Never implement Manual Edit as:

```text
DELETE reconstructed trade
INSERT reconstructed trade
```

The correct implementation is:

```text
Replace canonical executions
        ↓
Reconstruct
```

This preserves deterministic behavior.

================================================================================================================================

# 25. FAILURE-SAFETY RULE

================================================================================================================================

The most important Atomic Edit rule is:

```text
IF THE NEW EXECUTION SET CANNOT BE COMPLETELY PERSISTED,

THE OLD EXECUTION SET MUST REMAIN.
```

This is the reason the database transaction exists.

